 false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1519804887", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "54257295", "author": {"steamid": "76561198066211080", "personaname": "lyra ✧", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/lyramuci/", "num_games_owned": 569, "num_reviews": 8, "playtime_forever": 20135, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 20135, "last_played": 1717025513, "avatar": "298a86ee89d5ed9e313c6573697012667b7e7c6d"}, "language": "english", "review": "You play a dwarf. You mine stuff. You shoot bugs. You drink beer on a space rig. It sounds absurd and it [i]is[/i] absurd and that's exactly why it works.\n\nEvery class feels useful and none of them feel like dead weight. Whether you're playing Scout, Engineer, Driller, or Gunner, you're contributing something the team actually needs. The builds have real depth to them too once you start unlocking overclocks and experimenting.\n\nThe co-op is some of the best I've ever played. It doesn't matter if you're with friends or randoms, people just [i]get it[/i]. Everyone rocks and stones, everyone revives each other, everyone kicks barrels into the launch bay. The community around this game is genuinely wholesome for a shooter and it never gets old.\n\nGhost Ship Games deserves a lot of credit. They actually listen to the community, put out consistent updates, and haven't shoved predatory monetization into the game. The paid content that exists feels fair and optional. More devs should take notes.\n\nI've put hundreds of hours into this and I'm still not bored. That says everything.", "timestamp_created": 1563905245, "timestamp_updated": 1773394020, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.523809552192687988", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": 